From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] id3v2: one picture, of a size that can be held

Each APIC frame of an ID3v2 tag (in a WAV, an AIFF, an AAC stream...) was
read whole and kept with the others for as long as the file was open:
front, back and booklet pages of a few MB each add up to more than a small
player has. Only the first picture is read now, and only up to 4 MB (as
mov.c's FATHOM_COVER_MAX); the others are skipped, which read_apic() already
does for a picture it can't use. None is read for a context flagged
FATHOM_AVFMT_NO_PICTURES (see the mov patch), where read_apic() is given the
context.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [a small player's limits]

--- a/libavformat/id3v2.c
+++ b/libavformat/id3v2.c
@@ -607,7 +607,19 @@
     int64_t end               = avio_tell(pb) + taglen;
 
     if (taglen <= 4 || (!isv34 && taglen <= 6))
+        goto fail;
+
+    /* Fathom: one picture is all that is used, and never one over 4 MB
+     * (as mov.c's FATHOM_COVER_MAX): a second or a bigger one is passed
+     * over. Each used to be read whole and held with the others for as
+     * long as the file was open. */
+    if (taglen > 4 * 1024 * 1024 + 256)
         goto fail;
+    if (s && (s->flags & 0x40000000))   /* (FATHOM_AVFMT_NO_PICTURES, as mov.c: a file opened to be played) */
+        goto fail;
+    for (const ID3v2ExtraMeta *e = extra_meta->head; e; e = e->next)
+        if (!strcmp(e->tag, "APIC"))
+            goto fail;
 
     new_extra = av_mallocz(sizeof(*new_extra));
     if (!new_extra)
